Z||000004||skitime||07-02-2001||10:31 PM||||We have a factory CD 6 disc changer with a Grand AM cassette radio.  It is awesome.  The radio has the same red lighting including the equalizer.  The controls are on the radio so no stupid extra controls and the best part is punks are not going to break into a car to steal a cassette radio.  The changer is mounted in the front on the left wheel well.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||07-02-2001||11:06 PM||||I've got factory units in both of my cars.  My '85 has a nice late model Grand Am unit that lights up red, and has the red display.  My '84 has an older Pontiac unit out of a (guessing) early 90's Bonneville.  It's probably closer to looking like a factory fit, as it has the round grey knobs like the factory Fiero units, and lights up in red, but still has the green display.  Oddly enough, it also has a weather band!<P>I'm no stereo expert, but they sound OK to me and were a piece of cake to install.  <P>Good luck,<BR>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000006||Two88GTs||07-02-2001||11:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mope:<BR><B>if ya find a nice factory pontiac cd player for under 100 bucks let me know, I WANT ONE!<P>thanks<P>mope</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Surprisingly enough, eBay occasionally has good prices on late model Pontiac CD players. I bought one with a 7-band EQ eight months ago for $140(it was a good buy at the time) and brand new one with normal bass and treb controls for $82.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mope||07-03-2001||12:12 AM||||wait a sec...before i run and buy one i have some questions...i want the newest possible...<P>Would a monsoon system work?<BR>I heard a Bose system would be a pain to make work.<BR>So just a stock CD player rite? <P>or am i missing the whole boat?<P>Will any of these work with the stock sub???<P>thanks<BR>mope||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||07-03-2001||07:41 AM||||The Monsoon radio will work. That's what I have in my car. Make sure it's either an un-coded or you have the security code. You'll also need the adaptor for the connector and antenna. I bought mine from: <A HREF="http://www.newellelectronics.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.newellelectronics.com/</A>  for like $20. The radio looks like it was made for the car. It even lights up in the right color.<P>Good Luck,<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000009||baptistheart||07-03-2001||12:29 PM||||I have a 88 camaro cd player in mine works great was a snap to install cost $50||||reg||6
Z||000010||fierojunky||07-03-2001||01:25 PM||||I got a CD player out of a 99 Sunfire for $100 - only bad thing was they kept the wiring.  No biggie went to the Stero Shop and picked up the wiring and adapter.  Works great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
